 "comment": "Rounding, to the paisa, on three s.194C payees of a firm (lower rate 1%, higher rate 2%): 18 rows, 6 findings. Neem Movers: x01 (Rs 31,003.50) is taxed at 1% as Rs 310.04, the half paisa rounded up; x02 (Rs 69,000.49), which also takes the year's total over Rs 1,00,000, as Rs 690.00, the 0.49 of a paisa rounded down. After the crossing every credit is a tranche: x03 (49 paise) has no tax at 1% and 1 paisa at 2%; x04 (24 paise) has no tax at either rate; x05 (Rs 50) has tax of 50 paise at 1%, and 9 months at 1% on it, 4.5 paise, is 5, its still-not-deducted amount; x06 (Rs 49) has tax of 49 paise at 1%, and 9 months, 4.41 paise, is 4. x11 (Rs 9, 22 January) has tax of 9 paise at 1%, and its maximum is found only by trying every date of deduction: deducted that day, 9 months at 1.5% is 1.215 paise, 1; deducted the day after, 0.09 and 1.215 paise, 0 and 1; deducted on 1 June, 6 months at 1% and 4 months at 1.5% are 0.54 paise each, 1 and 1, so the maximum is 2. At 2% its tax is 18 paise and the maximum, 3, is reached on 1 March (0.54 and 1.89 paise) where the day itself and the day after give 2. The lower-rate finding lists 5 tranches and the higher-rate finding 6, because a tranche with no tax is left out of a finding while its figures stay. Oak Transit: x07 and x08 (Rs 31,050 each, both on 10 March) are one tranche of two credits; at 1% the tranche's still-not-deducted amount is Rs 43.47 and its own-date one, each credit rounded on its own, Rs 43.48, a paisa more, while its maximum is Rs 71.42 on both readings; at 2% its maximum is Rs 142.83 and its own-date maximum Rs 142.84. Palm Freight: x09 and x10 (Rs 31,075 each, same day) are one tranche; at 1% its still-not-deducted amount is Rs 43.51 and the own-date one Rs 43.50, a paisa less, and at 2% Rs 87.01 and Rs 87.02, a paisa more; at 2% its maximum is Rs 142.95 and its own-date maximum Rs 142.96.",
